[31m-## Installation[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Use Python 3.10 or newer and a PyTorch build suitable for your device.[m
[31m-Training data loading also requires NumPy and Pillow.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```bash[m
[31m-pip install -r requirements.txt[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Training data[m
[31m-```text[m
[31m-your_training_directory/[m
[31m-  I_alpha/sample.npy       H x W x 9: three RGB polarization views[m
[31m-  I_hat/sample.png         RGB total visible-light intensity[m
[31m-  delta_I_hat/sample.png   RGB intensity times degree of polarization[m
[31m-  P_A/sample.npy           Three-element airlight DoP vector[m
[31m-  P_T/sample.png           RGB transmitted-light DoP[m
[31m-  T/sample.png             RGB transmitted-light target[m
[31m-  gated/sample.png         Grayscale TGI observation[m
[31m-  ir_foggy/sample.png      Grayscale LWIR observation[m
[31m-  A_infinity/sample.png    RGB airlight target[m
[31m-  R/sample.png             RGB clear-radiance target[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-NPY values use the [0, 1] scale; PNG files use 8-bit values. The loader expands[m
[31m-the airlight DoP vector spatially and resizes the image fields with antialiased[m
[31m-bilinear interpolation.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Training[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The three configurations retain the training settings from the research source.[m
[31m-The entry point selects the configuration matching `--stage` automatically;[m
[31m-use `--config` to provide an edited copy.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-| Stage | Configuration | Epochs | Batch size | Initial learning rate |[m
[31m-| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |[m
[31m-| Transmission estimation | [`transmission.json`](configs/transmission.json) | 400 | 9 | 0.0005 |[m
[31m-| Radiance reconstruction | [`radiance.json`](configs/radiance.json) | 400 | 5 | 0.0001 |[m
[31m-| Joint training | [`joint.json`](configs/joint.json) | 400 | 4 | 0.0005 |[m
[31m-[m
[31m-All stages use 240 x 320 inputs, Adam with `betas=[0.5, 0.999]`, AMSGrad,[m
[31m-and zero weight decay. Each loss weight pair is `[L1, L2]`; stage-specific[m
[31m-weights are defined in the corresponding configuration. Convolution weights[m
[31m-are initialized from a zero-mean normal distribution with standard deviation 0.02,[m
[31m-linear weights use Xavier uniform initialization, and their biases are zeroed[m
[31m-before any checkpoint weights are loaded.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-The first two stages use `branch_decay`: at the end of each epoch after 300,[m
[31m-`MultiplicativeLR` multiplies the **current** learning rate by `2.5 - epoch / 200`.[m
[31m-The joint stage uses `constant`. This preserves the source schedule; the[m
[31m-branch multiplier is applied cumulatively, rather than as a linear interpolation[m
[31m-of the initial learning rate. The branch schedule is intended for 400 epochs[m
[31m-and requires a total below 500 to keep its multiplier positive.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Run from the repository root, replacing `PATH_TO_TRAIN_DATA` with your data path:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```bash[m
[31m-# Stage 1: transmission estimation[m
[31m-python train.py --stage transmission --data-root PATH_TO_TRAIN_DATA --output-dir outputs/transmission[m
[31m-[m
[31m-# Stage 2: radiance reconstruction[m
[31m-python train.py --stage radiance --data-root PATH_TO_TRAIN_DATA --output-dir outputs/radiance[m
[31m-[m
[31m-# Stage 3: joint training initialized from the two trained branches[m
[31m-python train.py --stage joint --data-root PATH_TO_TRAIN_DATA --transmission-weights outputs/transmission/transmission-last.pth --radiance-weights outputs/radiance/radiance-last.pth --output-dir outputs/joint[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Training saves `<stage>-last.pth` every `save_every` epochs and at the final[m
[31m-epoch. To resume an interrupted run, keep the same configuration and provide[m
[31m-`--resume`. To extend a completed run, increase `epochs` to the desired total;[m
[31m-keep the optimizer, loss, and scheduler settings unchanged:[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```bash[m
[31m-python train.py --stage joint --data-root PATH_TO_TRAIN_DATA --output-dir outputs/joint --resume outputs/joint/joint-last.pth[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-New outputs are ignored by Git. Checkpoints restore model, optimizer, scheduler,[m
[31m-and epoch state, without promising identical random sample order. Only[m
[31m-checkpoints created with this public naming scheme are supported.[m
[31m-[m
[31m-## Model interface[m
[31m-[m
[31m-```python[m
[31m-from models import DDPCFMD[m
[31m-[m
[31m-model = DDPCFMD(image_size=(240, 320))[m
[31m-# output = model(vlp, intensity, polarization_difference, lwir, tgi)[m
[31m-```[m
[31m-[m
[31m-Inputs are aligned floating-point NCHW tensors on the [0, 1] scale, with[m
[31m-9, 3, 3, 1, and 1 channels respectively. All inputs share batch size, spatial[m
[31m-size, dtype, and device. Each spatial dimension must be at least 80 and divisible[m
[31m-by 8. The output fields are `airlight_dop`, `transmission_dop`, `transmission`,[m
[31m-`tgi_transmission`, `airlight`, and `radiance`, each shaped `(N, 3, H, W)`.[m
[31m-Here, `transmission` is the transmitted-light image, not scalar transmittance.[m
